MID_SE_Anh_Sci_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Anh_Sci_C_001: Miss Anatolia! Would you allow me to regale you\nwith the legend of the hero Arago?
MID_SE_Anh_Sci_C_002: It will keep you captivated until dawn! Luckily,\nmy bed is open for the night, should you need one.
MID_SE_Anh_Sci_C_003: Weren't you just asking someone else for their\ncompany earlier?
MID_SE_Anh_Sci_C_004: Yes, and she turned me down, sending a frigid gale\nthrough my heart. I was hoping you'd warm it up.
MID_SE_Anh_Sci_C_005: After the auburn-haired woman I met last night,\nI would be eager to admire your cool black locks.
MID_SE_Anh_Sci_C_006: You had a one-night stand? If you're going to raise a\nchild together, shouldn't you maintain continuity?
MID_SE_Anh_Sci_C_007: In my village, it's strongly encouraged to be with one\nperson. It helps maintain the population.
MID_SE_Anh_Sci_C_008: My, my. To think the bride possesses such an\ninnocent heart!
MID_SE_Anh_Sci_C_009: Your purity is charming, indeed. But perhaps I can\nshare some advice you might find useful?
MID_SE_Anh_Sci_C_010: A union between people is not solely for the purpose\nof procreation. It should be rooted in love!
MID_SE_Anh_Sci_C_011: After all, when raising a child, it's better for there to\nbe love between the two. Do you understand so far?
MID_SE_Anh_Sci_C_012: You can raise a child without such things. But I\nsuppose it's helpful if it's there.
MID_SE_Anh_Sci_C_013: Yes, and one of the mysteries of love is that as easily\nas it flares up, it may cool down.
MID_SE_Anh_Sci_C_014: In those frigid times, partners may abandon each\nother, perhaps even leaving the child.
MID_SE_Anh_Sci_C_015: Such a thing should never happen, of course!\nBut how does one avoid it?
MID_SE_Anh_Sci_C_016: Hmm. Well, I suppose by taking proper precautions.
MID_SE_Anh_Sci_C_017: If you can predict what might cause a relationship\nto become cold, you can prevent it from happening.
MID_SE_Anh_Sci_C_018: Exactly so! And to make the most accurate possible\nprediction?
MID_SE_Anh_Sci_C_019: You would need to gather as many relevant cases as\npossible and use them as a basis for study.
MID_SE_Anh_Sci_C_020: Correct! One must accumulate data—have as many\nof these encounters as they can.
MID_SE_Anh_Sci_C_021: I suppose that makes sense... Perhaps.
MID_SE_Anh_Sci_C_022: I can prove it beyond a shadow of a doubt, after you\ngive me your hand tonight.
MID_SE_Anh_Sci_C_023: No, thank you. I'd like to learn more, but it doesn't\nneed to be with you.
MID_SE_Anh_Sci_C_024: Hmm, alright. But, ah...let me know if you'd like to\ndo some field research.
